course: dictionary
lesson: 15696
title: Togs: swimming costumes and clothes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one part of the world, so the words around them are your best clue. «Pack your togs, we are going to the pool.» You take things to the pool, so togs must be something you wear in the water.
explain: In Australia and Ireland, togs are swimming costumes. In the UK, the word has a second meaning: togs are clothes, especially clothes for a special purpose. «Get your togs on» means get dressed, and «your best togs» means your smartest clothes.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Ciara forgot her togs for swimming lessons.» Does swimming costume fit? Yes, and the sentence still makes sense. Context and a check like this will often solve a new word.
fact: Togs is a plural noun, and it is informal, so it is a relaxed everyday word.
fact: In Australia and Ireland, «togs» means swimming costumes.
fact: In the UK, «togs» can mean clothes for a special purpose, such as «football togs».
fact: «Get your togs on» means get dressed.
fact: «Togged up» means dressed up.
exercise: «Pack your togs, we are going to the pool.» What are togs in this sentence? | Clothes for the football pitch | *Swimming costumes | Shoes | Towels
exercise: «Get your togs on, we leave in five minutes.» What does this mean? | Go to sleep | Take a bath | *Get dressed | Wash the dishes
exercise: «The kids were togged up for the party.» Find and copy the word that means dressed up. | *togged | party | were | kids
test: «He put on his best togs for the wedding.» What are his best togs? | *His smartest clothes | A cheap cap | A pair of muddy boots | His swimming costume
test: In Ireland, what does «togs» mean in «Ciara forgot her togs for swimming lessons»? | A school bag | *A swimming costume | A cup of tea | A football
exam: Which phrase means the same as «get your togs on»? | Get undressed | Get lost | Get wet | *Get dressed
